    "abstract": "Illustrated parts breakdown of one cargo door latching station, showing both sensing channels, the latching rib, the intercostal and the cover hardware, common to the forward, aft and bulk doors.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure gives the parts breakdown of one cargo door latching station. Use it to order sensor bracket plates, latching intercostals and the cover hardware for any of the three cargo doors.",
      "figure_note": "The figure shows one station in section, and the station is repeated six times on each door. Items 10 to 30 are the first sensing channel and are fitted at every station. Items 40 to 60 are the second sensing channel and are an addition, not an alternate: on a duplicated station both channels are present, and the second channel takes the longer retaining pin because it sits on a taller standoff. Item 70 is the hardened intercostal and item 70A the spacer used at that position on the original standard. The callouts downstream of the intercostal were renumbered when the second channel was added, so a pick list raised against an earlier issue of this figure will not resolve item for item."
    },
